{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"1638e90fc89d5815f4f3092af098eedc249b4982c6f4df9bfd1f8cba70bb4304","digest":{"component_or_area":"git store lock management","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","_reclaim_if_stale_index_lock","index.lock","st_dev","st_ino","mtime"],"problem_keywords":["toctou","race condition","stale lock reclamation","inode replacement","file identity validation","index.lock"],"propositions":["_reclaim_if_stale_index_lock reads a lock file's mtime to judge staleness, then unconditionally removes the pathname without re-confirming the file's identity, creating a window for a peer to replace the stale lock with a fresh one","Between the initial stat and the unlink, an adversary can delete the stale lock and create a new live lock at the same pathname, causing rebar to unlink the peer's new lock instead of the stale one","No existing test exercises inode replacement during reclamation; current tests only cover a stationary stale lock and a young lock released later","The fix must re-validate file identity (device and inode) and mtime from the same stat call immediately before removal to ensure the removed file is the same stale file that was originally judged","A deterministic regression test must pause reclamation after the initial stat, replace the stale file with a fresh file, resume reclamation, and assert the replacement lock survives"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785824755869279590,"uuid":"53eb9616-c29b-4dda-8abe-15b61a423eaa"}